5.List three differences you noticed between running your Flutter app on the emulator versus a real Android device.For each difference, explain how it might
affect your development or testing process.\<br>\<br>\<em>\<strong>Hint:\</strong> Consider speed, device features, and debugging experience.\</emEmulator vs Real Android 
Device

 1. Speed
Emulator: May run slower depending on computer performance.
Real Device: Runs with the actual device performance.
Effect: Helps us test the real speed and performance of the app.

 2. Device Features
Emulator: Simulates features like camera, GPS, and sensors.
Real Device: Uses actual hardware features.
Effect: Helps us test hardware-related features more accurately.

3. Debugging
Emulator:Easy to test different Android versions and screen sizes.
Real Device: Helps find real-world device issues.
Effect: Testing on both gives better app reliability.
